# Work and trade between residents (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): chains. One asks after the other's work, or
# tells their own unasked; the other answers as their trade, their till, their purse and their temper make them; the
# first answers that in kind (work.reply, which reads how the news was told: conv.w7_tone), and some close it.
# Bosses give orders (work.order) or praise (work.praised), and hear pleas for pay (work.plea), for time off
# (work.leave) and worries about the shop (work.worry). Asked at the start of the day, one answers what's ahead
# (work.ahead); at its end, how it went (work.done); asked by their boss, they report (work.report).
#
# The beat that tells the news leaves two things for the reply (pair.mem, half an hour):
#   w7_tone: plain (nothing much), curt (a brush-off), low (the trade going badly), skint (their own money troubles),
#     hard (a hard day: hurt, weather, Restday work), high (the trade going well), good (a good day, or high hopes),
#     tired, busy, idle (a slack spell), bored, proud (denying bad news).
#   w7_from: a or b, who told it (a: told unasked; b: answered a question). With pair.boss this says whether the one
#     replying is the teller's boss or their hand: boss=a and from=b, or boss=b and from=a, is the boss replying.
# Closes: work.end (a plain last word), work.thanks (to kindness or an offer), work.retort (to a jibe).

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Asking after the work

rule w7_ask_trade
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=acquaintances|friends other.business=thriving|steady|failing pair.boss=no
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say How's trade? | Selling much? | Is the till singing or sulking? | Business keeping you? | Much custom this week?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_trade_close
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=friends|family|spouses other.business=thriving|steady|failing self.warmth=warm
does ask.after
cooldown 1d
say And how's business, #pet#? Truly, now. | How's the trade treating you, #pet#? | Tell me straight. How are you doing for custom?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_rival
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk pair.band=rivals other.business=thriving|steady|failing
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say Still open, are you? | Heard your shelves were full. Nobody buying? | Keeping the doors open, I see. Just.
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_workmate
when concept=talk.work other.working=yes pair.boss=no
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say How's your end going? | Getting anywhere with it? | How's it looking your side? | Making headway?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_chatty
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk self.talk=chatty pair.band=acquaintances|friends other.working=yes
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say Now then, what are you at? Tell me everything. | Ooh, what's that you're doing? Is it hard? | Don't let me stop you, but how's it all going?
then other: work.answer

## Broad askings: almost anyone, to almost anyone (few criteria, many words)

rule w7_ask_any
when concept=talk.work
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say How's the work? | Keeping busy? | Much on? | How goes it? | Getting on all right?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_day
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=day
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Half the day gone already. How's yours? | Got much done? | What's the day thrown at you so far?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_any_friend
when concept=talk.work pair.band=friends|family|spouses
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say How's it going, #pet#? Really. | Are they working you hard? | Tell me about your day.
then other: work.answer

## Same trade, asking shop talk

rule w7_ask_smith
when concept=talk.work self.job=smith other.job=smith pair.band!=rivals
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say How's your iron behaving? | Fire drawing well your end? | Many orders in?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_baker
when concept=talk.work self.job=baker other.job=baker pair.band!=rivals
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Did your dough rise this morning? Mine sulked. | How's the oven treating you? | Selling out, or feeding the pigeons?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_farmer
when concept=talk.work self.job=farmer other.job=farmer pair.band!=rivals
does ask.after
cooldown 1d
say How's your ground? | Anything coming up your side? | How are the beasts?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_fisher
when concept=talk.work self.job=fisher other.job=fisher
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Fish biting for you? | Any luck out there? | How were the nets?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_guard
when concept=talk.work self.role=guard other.role=guard
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Quiet on your beat? | Anything doing? | Trouble your way?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_healer
when concept=talk.work self.job=healer other.job=healer
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say How are your patients? | Many at your door today? | Is that cough still going round your end?
then other: work.answer

rule w7_ask_merchant
when concept=talk.work self.role=merchant other.role=merchant pair.band!=rivals
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Moving much? | How's the counting going? | Selling, or just standing?
then other: work.answer

## The start of the day and its end (work.ahead, work.done)

rule w7_ask_before_shift
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk|talk.day other.shift=before
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Off to it, then? | Ready for the day? | What's waiting for you today?
then other: work.ahead

rule w7_ask_any_dawn
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=dawn
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Up early as ever. Big day? | What's on for today? | You look half asleep. Long day ahead?
then other: work.ahead

rule w7_ask_after_shift
when concept=talk.work|talk.smalltalk|talk.day other.shift=after
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Long day? | Finished for the day, then? | How did the day go? | Knocked off at last?
then other: work.done

rule w7_ask_any_dusk
when concept=talk.work|talk.day here.time=dusk|night
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Done for the day? | Was it a long one? | Getting home at last?
then other: work.done

## The boss asks how it's going (work.report)

rule w7_ask_boss_checks
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=calm|even
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say How are you getting on? | All going to plan? | Anything you need from me?
then other: work.report

rule w7_ask_boss_short
when concept=talk.work pair.boss=a other.working=yes self.temper=short|nervy
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Is it done yet? | Why's that not finished? | What have you been doing all this while?
then other: work.report

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Answering about the work (work.answer)

rule w7_ans_plain
when concept=work.answer
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Steady. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Can't grumble. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Same as ever. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Ticking over. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Oh, you know. #work.capitalize#.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_short
when concept=work.answer temper=short
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=curt w7_from=b} Busy. Why? | {w7_tone=curt w7_from=b} It'd go faster without questions. | {w7_tone=curt w7_from=b} Fine. Is that all? | {w7_tone=curt w7_from=b} Don't ask.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_merry
when concept=work.answer humour=merry
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Oh, wonderful. Nothing's caught fire yet. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Grand! I've only cursed twice. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Splendid. Ask me again in an hour.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_dry
when concept=work.answer humour=dry
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Thrilling. I can hardly contain myself. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Much as yesterday. And the day before that. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} It's #work#. It does what it does.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_guarded
when concept=work.answer honesty=guarded
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Well enough. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Oh, this and that. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} It goes. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Can't complain. Wouldn't, if I could.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_ambitious
when concept=work.answer drive=ambitious
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=good w7_from=b} Well, and it'll be better. I've plans. | {w7_tone=good w7_from=b} Good. Not good enough. Not yet. | {w7_tone=good w7_from=b} Growing. You'll see.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_content
when concept=work.answer drive=content
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Suits me fine. Always has. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} No complaints. The work's honest. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Same as my #dad# had it. That's no bad thing.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_restless
when concept=work.answer drive=restless
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=bored w7_from=b} Same as ever. That's the trouble. | {w7_tone=bored w7_from=b} I could do it in my sleep. Some days I do. | {w7_tone=bored w7_from=b} Dull as ditchwater, if you want the truth.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_quiet
when concept=work.answer talk=quiet
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Fine. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Mm. Good. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Going.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_chatty
when concept=work.answer talk=chatty
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Oh, where to start! First the cart was late, then the cart was early, then... | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Busy, busy. Did I tell you about the new stool? It wobbles. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Good! Mostly. You'd not believe the day I've had.
then other: work.reply

## The till

rule w7_ans_steady
when concept=work.answer business=steady
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Steady. Pays the rent. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Not rich, not ruined. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Regulars keep me going. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Enough coming in, just.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_failing
when concept=work.answer business=failing
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=low w7_from=b} Badly. Nobody's buying. | {w7_tone=low w7_from=b} Four days without a sale. I've started counting flies. | {w7_tone=low w7_from=b} I'll be shut by the next moon, the way it's going. | {w7_tone=low w7_from=b} I count the till and it doesn't take long.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_thriving
when concept=work.answer business=thriving
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=high w7_from=b} Run off my paws! | {w7_tone=high w7_from=b} Can't keep the shelves full. | {w7_tone=high w7_from=b} Best month I've had. Touch wood. | {w7_tone=high w7_from=b} I've a waiting list. Me!
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_failing_proud
when concept=work.answer business=failing temper=short warmth=cold|reserved
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=proud w7_from=b} Fine. It's fine. | {w7_tone=proud w7_from=b} Never better. | {w7_tone=proud w7_from=b} It'll pick up. It always picks up. | {w7_tone=proud w7_from=b} Mind your own till.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_thriving_guarded
when concept=work.answer business=thriving honesty=guarded|sly
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Oh, slow. Terribly slow. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Mustn't grumble. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Getting by, getting by.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_owes
when concept=work.answer owes=yes business=steady|failing
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=low w7_from=b} I'm working for the lender, not for me. | {w7_tone=low w7_from=b} Everything I take goes out the door again. Debts. | {w7_tone=low w7_from=b} I'd be fine if I didn't owe half the street.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_destitute
when concept=work.answer wealth=destitute
does answer.how
priority 2
say {w7_tone=skint w7_from=b} I'm working and still can't eat. Tell me how that's right. | {w7_tone=skint w7_from=b} There isn't enough work in the world to dig me out. | {w7_tone=skint w7_from=b} Every penny's gone before I've earned it.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_tired
when concept=work.answer tired=yes working=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=tired w7_from=b} I'm asleep on my paws. | {w7_tone=tired w7_from=b} #tired.capitalize#. Ask me after I've slept. | {w7_tone=tired w7_from=b} Long. Very long. And not done yet. | {w7_tone=tired w7_from=b} I could lie down on this floor.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_before
when concept=work.answer shift=before
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Not started. Don't remind me. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Off to it now. Wish me luck. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Ask me tonight.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_after
when concept=work.answer shift=after
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Done for the day, and glad of it. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Finished. Feet up soon. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} It's behind me now. That's the best part.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_day_off
when concept=work.answer shift=day_off
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=good w7_from=b} Not today! Day off. Don't spoil it. | {w7_tone=good w7_from=b} I'm not thinking about it. Not one thought. | {w7_tone=good w7_from=b} Ask me tomorrow. Today I'm a wolf of leisure.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_hurt
when concept=work.answer injured=light working=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Working one-pawed today. Took a knock. | {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Slower than usual. It's the shoulder. | {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Fine, if I don't lift anything. Which is the whole job.
then other: work.reply

## The day's kind

rule w7_ans_market_merchant
when concept=work.answer here.day=market role=merchant
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Market day! Don't ask me now. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Haven't sat since dawn. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Everyone wants everything, and all at once.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_market_food
when concept=work.answer here.day=market job=baker|cook|brewer|innkeeper
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Market day. Cleared out by noon, I'll be. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Feeding half the county today. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Every stallholder wants feeding and every farmer wants a drink.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_restday
when concept=work.answer here.day=rest working=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Working Restday. Again. | {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Restday, they call it. Not for me. | {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} #bc_somebody_has_to#
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_festival
when concept=work.answer here.day=festival working=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Working through the festival. Can you hear them out there? | {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Everyone's dancing but me. | {w7_tone=hard w7_from=b} Feast days are work days, for some of us.
then other: work.reply

## Masters, apprentices, the Houses

rule w7_ans_apprentice
when concept=work.answer apprentice=yes
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Learning. Slowly. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} I've ruined less than yesterday. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} My master says I'm improving. Then sighs.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_master
when concept=work.answer master=yes
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Good, but the apprentice will be the death of me. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Teaching takes twice as long as doing. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Well. My pupil's coming on.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_house
when concept=work.answer self.house job!=noble
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} The House keeps us busy. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Steady. The House always has work. Pays when it pays. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Can't complain. It's House work. Regular.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_greatly
when concept=work.answer self.house=greatly_house working=yes job!=noble
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Brick, lime, brick, lime. Greatly sells and I carry. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Another load of tiles for the Greatly Yard. My shoulders know every one. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Greatly's paint in my fur again. Never comes out.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fell
when concept=work.answer self.house=house_fell working=yes job!=noble
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Must in everything. House Fell's got casks stacked to the roof. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Wine, brandy, cordial. Fell wants all of it yesterday. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Fruit's wet. Fell says press it anyway.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_grayrock
when concept=work.answer self.house=grayrock_hall working=yes job!=noble
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Grayrock's wharf doesn't sleep. Nor do we, much. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Cargo in, cargo out. Grayrock counts every bale. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Wet, loud, and Grayrock's steward watching.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_mossgrave
when concept=work.answer self.house=mossgrave_court|timberland_court working=yes job!=noble
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Soot to the elbows. Timberland iron, this week. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} The forges roar and Timberland pays. That's the deal. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Iron, iron and more iron. Timberland's never short of work.
then other: work.reply

## By trade

rule w7_ans_smith
when concept=work.answer job=smith
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Iron's poor this month. Brittle. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Hinges, nails, hinges. Never a sword. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Singed the same paw three times. Otherwise good.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_baker
when concept=work.answer job=baker
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Up since the small hours. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Dough sulked this morning, but it came round. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Flour in my ears, flour in my fur. Same as ever.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_brewer
when concept=work.answer job=brewer
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} The new batch is working. You can smell it from the street. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Barrels to scrub. Always barrels to scrub. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Good brew this time. Don't tell anyone.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_innkeeper
when concept=work.answer job=innkeeper
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Full last night, and not one of them paid on time. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Rooms let, stools broken. A good week. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} The cellar's full and the taproom's empty. Wrong way round.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_guard
when concept=work.answer role=guard
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Quiet. I like quiet. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Two drunks and a lost goat. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Boots wearing through. Otherwise fine.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_soldier
when concept=work.answer job=soldier
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Drill, polish, drill. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} They march us up the hill and march us down again. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Waiting. Soldiering's mostly waiting.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer
when concept=work.answer job=farmer
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} The ground's good, if the sky behaves. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Weeds grow faster than I can pull them. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Beasts are fed. That's a day.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_spring
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=spring
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Sowing. My back's in two pieces. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Seed's in. Now we wait and pray. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Ploughing till dark, every day.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_summer
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=summer
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Haymaking. Every dry day counts. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Hoeing. Endless hoeing. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Watching the sky and the barley, both.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_autumn
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=autumn
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Harvest. Talk to me when it's in the barn. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Every paw in the field and still not enough. | {w7_tone=busy w7_from=b} Good yield this year. Or it will be, if the rain holds off.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_farmer_winter
when concept=work.answer job=farmer here.season=winter
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=idle w7_from=b} Mending fences and staring at the snow. | {w7_tone=idle w7_from=b} Winter. Nothing to do but feed the beasts and worry. | {w7_tone=idle w7_from=b} Sharpening everything I own, twice.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder
when concept=work.answer job=herder
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Flock's well. One wanders, but there's always one. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Counted them twice. Same number both times. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Ewes are fat and the shepherds are lazy.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder_spring
when concept=work.answer job=herder here.season=spring
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=tired w7_from=b} Lambing. I've not slept in a week. | {w7_tone=tired w7_from=b} Twins in the night, both living. | {w7_tone=tired w7_from=b} Up to my elbows in ewe. Don't shake my paw.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_herder_winter
when concept=work.answer job=herder here.season=winter
does answer.how
priority 1
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Hay's going faster than I'd like. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Brought them all down off the hill before the snow. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Breaking ice on the troughs every morning.
then other: work.reply

rule w7_ans_fisher
when concept=work.answer job=fisher
does answer.how
say {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Nets came up half full. Or half empty, depending who's counting. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Fish are deep today. Sulking, like the rest of us. | {w7_tone=plain w7_from=b} Good catch. Smell my paws if you don't believe me.
